course: dictionary
lesson: 14480
title: Patented: protected or just special?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their form to fit the sentence. Patent is a word for an official right, and patented is its past form: «The inventor patented her new bicycle lock.» This means she got an official right to make and sell her lock.
explain: Patented can also describe a thing, as in «The patented lock cannot be copied.» Here it means protected by a patent, so nobody else may copy or sell it for a number of years. Look at the words around it to check.
explain: People also use patented as a joke. «Dad's patented pancake flip» is not a real legal right. It means a special move that only Dad does, the way he always does it. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: A patent is an official right that says only the inventor may make or sell an invention for a number of years.
fact: «Patented» means got a patent, or protected by a patent.
fact: Patent, patents, patented and patenting are all forms of the same verb.
fact: In jokes, «patented» means special and typical of one person, like «Dad's patented pancake flip».
fact: When you meet a new word, ask: is this the legal meaning or the joking one? The sentence will show you.
exercise: «The inventor patented her new bicycle lock so nobody else could sell it.» What does patented mean here? | Painted the lock bright red | Gave the lock away for free | *Got an official right that lets only her make and sell the lock | Lost the lock in the park
exercise: «Dad's patented pancake flip never fails.» What does patented mean in this joke? | Made of paper and patent leather | Very slow and boring | Sent to a patent office for checking | *Special and typical of Dad alone
exercise: Which word is the past tense of the verb patent? | patenting | patents | patent | *patented
test: «The company sells a patented design of water bottle.» What does patented mean in this sentence? | Heavy and hard to carry | *Protected by a patent, so no one else may copy the design | Painted in bright colours | Full of holes and leaks
test: What is a patent? | *An official right that lets only the inventor make or sell an invention for a number of years | A tiny sweet made in an old shop | A type of shoe | A map of a city
exam: Which meaning fits the joke «Mum's patented hug can fix any bad day»? | Got an official right to sell hugs | Made of soft cloth | Protected by a patent office in London | *Special and typical of Mum, a hug only she gives this way
